00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:25.019
question here, number 132. "A solid
cylinder of mass 2 kg and radius

00:07:25.019 --> 00:07:32.999
4 cm is rotating about its axis
at the rate of 3 rpm." So I'll draw a

00:07:32.999 --> 00:07:40.849
little cylinder here and it's rotating
about its axis there. Now, what do we know?

00:07:40.849 --> 00:07:45.749
We know what it is rotating at and we
know that we're slowing it down to a

00:07:45.749 --> 00:07:54.929
stop. So we know that our final omega (ω_f) at
angular velocity is going to be equal to

00:07:54.929 --> 00:08:02.879
zero and our initial omega is going to
be equal to 3 rpm. Now that's

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.980
revolutions per minute so to convert
that into radians per second we would go

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:15.460
three times two pi over 60 (3 × 2π/60), that would be six pi over 60 (6π/60)

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:23.080
which we could cancel to pi over ten (π/10) rads per second.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.260
Now in the question
we're being asked about the torque

00:08:26.279 --> 00:08:31.319
required to bring it to a stop. So
hopefully something that we've

00:08:31.319 --> 00:08:38.899
remembered going into this exam is a way
to find torque (τ), and that is in rotational

00:08:38.899 --> 00:08:45.510
mechanics, the 'I', so the moment of inertia
times the angular acceleration (α).

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:51.060
Now if you've also memorized, so yeah
it's a lot to cram into your mind, but if

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:55.680
you've also memorized the moment of
inertia for a cylinder rotating like

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:03.540
this, you would know that it is: m R squared over two (mR²/2). I guess that kind of is

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:08.820
fair enough to know if you're studying
physics because you do a lot of moment

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:12.780
of inertia questions with different
shapes but still you you wouldn't want

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:17.440
to be doubting yourself on whether
you've got that one correct. But anyway, it's

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:24.220
'I' times the acceleration. Now we have
the mass in the radius so all we need

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:30.440
now is this angular acceleration or in
this case it would be decelerating to

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:37.710
zero. Now what we need to know to be able
to get that is a kinematic equation for

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:43.860
rotational motion. Now the one that in
particular we're going to need to use is

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:53.630
that the final angular velocity squared
is equal to the initial squared plus two

00:09:53.630 --> 00:10:02.190
alpha times theta. So that's the you know,
basically the distance or the angular

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:06.900
distance you've moved through, the
angular acceleration. So if you're not

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:12.090
already doing a lot of rotational
mechanics problems you be like where on

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.830
earth did this come from but if you're
familiar with kinematics at all this is

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:23.580
sort of an analogue to one of the linear
kinematic equations and again I feel

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:28.020
like it's something you need to memorize
for the sake of this exam which you know

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:31.560
it would be easier if they had a formula
sheet or something like that but of

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:36.210
course this is a pretty difficult exam
so let's see if we can plug things in

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:48.159
here and solve for our acceleration.
That should be the initial zero is pi

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:03.820
we've got theta being 2 pi times 2 pi
because it was 2 pi revolutions but each

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:12.070
revolution itself was 2 pi. We can solve
this and I'll just write it up here by

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:18.450
taking that over there and dividing by
these numbers you would end up with

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:32.540
and then plugging that into here with
two kgs and four centimeters squared

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:43.780
you'd end up with your torque being equal
to two times ten to the minus six Newtons,

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:50.240
and that corresponds to this answer to
here. That was a little involved and

